\title{Lagrangian Multiplier Smoothing Splines}
\description{
Implements Lagrangian multiplier smoothing splines for flexible nonparametric regression and function estimation. Provides tools for fitting, prediction, and inference using a constrained optimization approach to enforce smoothness. Supports generalized linear models, Weibull accelerated failure time (AFT) models, quadratic programming constraints, and customizable working-correlation structures, with options for parallel fitting. The core spline construction builds on Ezhov et al. (2018) \doi{10.1515/jag-2017-0029}. Generalized linear model background follows McCullagh & Nelder (1989) <ISBN:978-0412317606>. Quadratic-programming and SQP details follow Goldfarb & Idnani (1983) \doi{10.1007/BF02591962} and Nocedal & Wright (2006) \doi{10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5}. For smoothing spline and penalized spline background, see Wahba (1990) \doi{10.1137/1.9781611970128} and Wood (2017) \doi{10.1201/9781315370279}. For variance-component and correlation-parameter estimation, see Searle et al. (2006) <ISBN:978-0470009598>. The default multivariate partitioning step uses k-means clustering as in MacQueen (1967) and follows the same general partition-first motivation used in recent applied hybrid modeling examples such as Kisi et al. (2025) \doi{10.1038/s41598-025-91234-0}.
}
